       "text": "Your own dwell is marked on the curve, and the status line turns it into a sentence — how good it is, and how much better the best dwell would be.<br/><br/>Rough guide: <b>below 5 %</b> means differences between conditions will be measurable; <b>5–20 %</b> is usable for a large effect; above that the experiment is unlikely to answer the question.<br/><br/>Two honest limits. Each point is <b>itself a Monte-Carlo estimate</b> — about 10 % at the default repeat count — so the position of the minimum is an order of magnitude and not a value to dial in. And precision is quoted <b>per frame count, not per unit time</b>: a slower scan in this comparison is also a longer acquisition, so read the table's implied line and frame times before choosing.<br/><br/>The <b>?</b> button has the rest.",
